# =============================================================================
# NicksFix — .gitignore
# =============================================================================

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---- Virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---- IDE / editor ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---- OS cruft ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Claude Code local state (machine-specific; not team config) ----
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- Downloaded / auto-fetched binaries (re-fetched by the setup flow) ----
bin/platform-tools/

# ---- Runtime-generated device output (real backups, screenshots, PII) ----
# Acquisitions pull real user data off a device. The Browse button allows any
# output path, so these patterns are unanchored on purpose — they catch stray
# acquisition output anywhere in the tree, not just the default location.
/backups/
backups/
**/DCIM/
**/itunes_backup/
**/crash_reports/
**/apps_inventory.json
logical_*/
logical_plus_*/
prfs_*/
ffs_*/
*.tar
temp_shot.png
*.ips
*.crash

# Device media formats — never belongs in the repo
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.mov
*.MOV
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.JPG
*.png
*.mp4

# Exception: project artwork IS tracked (logos are SVG, but keep this explicit
# in case raster assets are added later).
!resources/logos/**
# App icon: logo.png is the master art, app.png/app.ico are generated from it.
!resources/logo.png
!resources/app.png

# ---- Auth server: entire directory excluded from the public repo, not just
# secrets — deploy scripts, VM host details, and infra layout don't belong
# in a public NicksFix checkout either.
server/

# ---- Internal project tracker (full history, machine/account specifics) ----
# The public-facing summary lives in README.md and IS committed.
RevLog.md

# ---- Local env / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
*.local.json

# ---- PyInstaller build output ----
build/
dist/

# ---- Packaged release artifacts (built, then uploaded to GitHub Releases) ----
# The zip is a build output, not source — it lives on the Releases page, not in git.
RootForgeKit-*.zip

# Superpowers SDD scratch workspace
.superpowers/

# =============================================================================
# Agent / AI-CLI configuration — internal, not for the public
# =============================================================================
# These describe how coding agents work on this repo (instructions, label
# vocabularies, issue-tracker wiring, local tool state). Useful to whoever
# maintains the project, noise — or a roadmap leak — to everyone else.

# Assistant-owned dot-directories: Claude Code, Kilo, Gemini CLI, Cursor,
# Copilot, Windsurf, Aider, OpenCode, Amp. One rule for the whole family —
# an assistant's workspace is machine-local state, never source.
.claude/
.kilo/
.gemini/
.cursor/
.copilot/
.windsurf/
.aider*
.opencode/
.agents/
.scratch/
amp/

# Assistant-authored markdown: AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md / KILO.md
# are per-machine instructions, and anything an assistant writes under
# docs/ is scratch. README.md is the one public-facing document and stays.
*.md
!README.md

docs/agents/

# =============================================================================
# pytmobiledevice3 project — maintained separately, lives outside this repo
# =============================================================================
# Moved to Desktop\Relocate. Listed so a stray copy never lands back in git.
pymobile3_gui/
build_pymobile3/
dist_pymobile3/
